WHAT: Adds #[arithmetic(unchecked)] to all crypto precompile wrappers in
std::evm::crypto (ec_add, ec_mul, ec_pairing, sha256, modexp, ecrecover).

WHY: Crypto precompile wrappers do pointer arithmetic to set up staticcall
input buffers. These are bounded by fixed sizes (128, 96, 192 bytes) and
can never overflow. The checked arithmetic generates unnecessary uaddo
instructions in hot inner loops of the verifier.

GAS IMPACT: -3608 gas total.
  verifier/plonkVerify: -3498 (-1.0%)
  verifier/groth16Verify: -110
  Other contracts: no change (don't use crypto precompiles)

TEAM NOTES: Targeted optimization for the verifier. The plonk verifier
calls ec_add 8 times, ec_mul 10 times, modexp 6 times — each with 2-3
uaddo instructions from buffer pointer arithmetic. Eliminating ~50 uaddo
instructions saves ~3500 gas. This demonstrates that #[arithmetic(unchecked)]
on provably-safe std library functions is a reliable optimization pattern.
